{'symbol': 'UNH', 'date': '2022-04-07 09:00:00', 'title': "ADDITIONAL $100 MILLION INVESTMENT IN HOUSING BOLSTERS UNITEDHEALTH GROUP'S EFFORTS TO ADDRESS SOCIAL DETERMINANTS AND ACHIEVE BETTER HEALTH OUTCOMES", 'text': "MINNETONKA, MINN.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--UNITEDHEALTH GROUP (NYSE: UNH) ANNOUNCED AN ADDITIONAL $100 MILLION INVESTMENT IN THE HEALTH & HOUSING FUND — A PARTNERSHIP WITH STEWARDS OF AFFORDABLE HOUSING FOR THE FUTURE (SAHF) AND NATIONAL AFFORDABLE HOUSING TRUST (NAHT). THE ANNOUNCEMENT BRINGS THE COMPANY'S TOTAL INVESTMENTS IN AFFORDABLE HOUSING TO NEARLY $800 MILLION, RESULTING IN THE CREATION OF NEARLY 19,000 HOMES FOR INDIVIDUALS AND FAMILIES STRUGGLING WITH HOUSING INSECURITY, MORE THAN 1,000"}